    <!-- Phase tips: one is picked per day, deterministically. Pools may differ in length
         between languages; the picker takes the index modulo whatever it loads. -->
    <string-array name="phase_tips_menstrual">
        <item>Cramps and low energy are likely. Care without pressure lands better right now — a hot water bottle, tea, a blanket, a film together — and don\'t push for intimacy unless she brings it up.</item>
        <item>Her body is recovering, so there may be less energy than usual. Quietly taking over the household chores is real support, no speech required.</item>
        <item>Discomfort and irritability these days are physiology, not about you. Don\'t take sharpness personally.</item>
        <item>A good moment to offer a hot water bottle or a painkiller if she forgot, rather than waiting to be asked.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="phase_tips_follicular">
        <item>Energy and mood usually climb. Good time for active dates, new ideas and plans together.</item>
        <item>Drive and focus are often on the rise — a convenient moment to talk through shared plans or start something new together.</item>
        <item>Mood is usually steady and open. A good time for conversations you have been putting off.</item>
        <item>A good window for something active — a walk, sport, a trip. There is usually energy to spare.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="phase_tips_ovulatory">
        <item>Often the peak of energy and libido. A fitting moment for romance and closeness — but go by how she feels right now, not by the phase alone.</item>
        <item>Confidence and sociability are frequently at their highest these days — a good time for something memorable together.</item>
        <item>The peak of the cycle guarantees no mood — it only shifts the odds slightly. The final word is always how she actually feels.</item>
        <item>If it has been a while since a proper date, these days are statistically a better bet for suggesting one.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="phase_tips_luteal">
        <item>Mood swings and PMS are possible towards the end of this phase. More patience, less criticism — a quiet evening usually goes down better than an ambitious plan.</item>
        <item>Cravings, tiredness and sensitivity to small things are ordinary companions of this phase, not grounds for an argument.</item>
        <item>A good time to slow down together — fewer loud plans, more quiet time side by side.</item>
        <item>If she is suddenly sharper or more closed off than usual, that is more often the phase than anything about you.</item>
    </string-array>
